<title>JAPAN: Japan small banks lent 6.69 trln yen to non-banks.</title>
<headline>Japan small banks lent 6.69 trln yen to non-banks.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese financial institutions other than the 20 major banks have made a total of 6.69 trillion yen in loans to non-bank lending institutions, a senior finance ministry official said on Friday.</p>
<p>Kimio Yamaguchi, director-general of the Ministry of Finance's Banking Bureau, made the statement at a parliamentary budget committee session.</p>
</text>
